1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,200
Event delivery is complex, and the biggest risk isn't change itself.

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:08,700
It's losing track of what that change actually breaks.

3
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:13,200
Here is a solution for OnCueX, built on Converge.AI.

4
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:16,600
OnCueX manages high-stakes innovation events,

5
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:20,100
but their core team struggles with fragmented information

6
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:22,500
hidden in emails and spreadsheets.

7
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:28,100
They need a scalable, consistent way to handle changes without accidental oversights.

8
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:31,700
When a venue moves, the plan often looks correct on the surface

9
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:34,700
while critical dependencies fail silently.

10
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:39,600
OnCueX needs to know exactly which commitments remain supported and which do not,

11
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:41,500
before making promises.

12
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:43,300
Compare the two workflows.

13
00:00:43,300 --> 00:00:48,800
Currently, a venue change requires manual, error-prone rechecks by the whole team.

14
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:52,700
Our approach turns that process into a single reviewed command

15
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:56,000
that instantly flags only affected commitments.

16
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,600
By computing impact based on specific dependencies,

17
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:03,400
unrelated work remains untouched and verified.

18
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:06,200
Notice how the photography commitment stays green

19
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:10,400
while other impacted items clearly show they need a revisit.

20
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:13,200
We don't use abstract status scores.

21
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:16,700
The system provides a clear, narrative view of the conflict,

22
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:20,400
the reason it exists, and the specific fix required,

23
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:23,700
allowing producers to recheck the plan with one click.

24
00:01:23,700 --> 00:01:27,100
The system never automatically approves anything.

25
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:33,200
Readiness is computed, but acceptance is a deliberate, recorded act by a human lead,

26
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:36,600
ensuring accountability for every revision of the plan.

27
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:40,300
We separate passing comments from formal commands,

28
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:44,600
ensuring that only deliberate changes trigger a plan reassessment.

29
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:46,900
The AI is strictly bounded.

30
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:49,700
It reads the brief and drafts requirements,

31
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:53,400
but it has no code path to alter the plan itself.

32
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:58,600
It invents nothing and leaves unknowns clearly marked for human resolution.

33
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:02,500
The impact is real, faster, more reliable planning,

34
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:08,600
predictable delivery within budget, and operational clarity that survives staff turnover.

35
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:11,600
Note, however, that these are early observations,

36
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:14,400
not yet benchmarked against historic data.

37
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,600
Our architecture fits their workflow by design.

38
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:22,800
Read-only imports, authenticated roles, and a tunable dependency graph.

39
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:28,200
We validate these improvements through real projects before claiming broad capacity gains.

40
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:32,600
This is a deployed live application, not a laptop prototype.

41
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:36,900
You can explore the full event management tabs, test the persistence,

42
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:40,600
and see the validated model calls for yourself at the provided address.

43
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:45,200
The model does not make final decisions or verify real-world permits.

44
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:47,300
Safety remains in human hands.

45
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:51,200
Plans change, but your record should always notice.

46
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:56,000
Readiness is computed from evidence and sign-offs are held by the lead.

47
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
We invite you to explore the source and the live app.
